        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: o arraial",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o arraial — \"the open-air party (at a festival)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No verão, há arraiais em todos os bairros. In summer, there are street parties in every neighbourhood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In June the city quarters fill with arraiais, music and grilled sardines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of arraial is not settled; it first meant a military camp and is usually linked with real 'army camp', but EtymDB has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
